Use of Generative AI
We used Claude (Anthropic) as a tutor while working on this deliverable. We asked it to guide us without giving complete solutions. We used it for:
•	Setup and tools: creating a Frost client ID file and excluding it with .gitignore, collaborating on a shared GitHub repository, selecting a Python kernel and installing packages in VS Code.
•	Understanding the Frost API: how to find endpoints and elements, how the JSON response is structured, and the difference between the sources, observations and availableTimeSeries endpoints.
•	Debugging: explaining error messages (NameError, KeyError, 401 Unauthorized) and problems caused by cells being run out of order.
•	Data issues: discovering that Frost returns two versions of daily values (PT0H/PT6H for mean and PT0H/PT18H for max temperature), and that the end date in referencetime is exclusive. The AI provided the code line for filtering on timeOffset and the fix for the date range.
•	Code provided by the AI: a temporary cell to build df_temp for 2025 (adapted from our own Task 3 code), and line-by-line comments explaining our Task 3 and Task 4 code.
•	Presentation: suggested talking points for the video.
All analysis choices, results and interpretations were reviewed and decided by us, and we went through the code ourselves to make sure we understand it.
